      bodyEn: [
        { t: "p", v: "For a long time, 'using AI' meant pasting a prompt and hoping. That works for a demo — not for production. What changed the game was treating AI as just another orchestrated service, with clear inputs, outputs and contracts." },
        { t: "h2", v: "n8n as the nervous system" },
        { t: "p", v: "I put n8n at the center: it receives webhooks from the app, decides which agent to trigger, calls the LLM and returns a structured response. Everything is versioned and dockerized, so the same flow runs identically in any environment." },
        { t: "h2", v: "MCP for real context" },
        { t: "p", v: "The Model Context Protocol solved the most annoying problem: giving the agent controlled access to real data (Supabase, n8n flows) without exposing the whole house. Agents read and write entities through explicit tools — no loose SQL coming out of a model." },
        { t: "quote", v: "AI accelerates the work; engineering judgment decides what ships to production." },
        { t: "p", v: "The result is a system where switching from OpenAI to Anthropic or Gemini is a config change, not a rewrite. No vendor lock-in, with observability in between." },
      ],
